%% Figure 4.2 — Verdict-Memory Fingerprint and Acknowledgement Flow
%% Appears in: Chapter 4, Section 4.2.5 (The Verdict-Memory)
%% Render to: ../fig_4_2_llm_classes.png
%% NOTE: a change to the signature, prompt_version, or model yields a new
%% fingerprint so the prior acknowledgement lapses; high/critical are never suppressed.
flowchart LR
  V["Verdict<br/>(severity, signature)"] --> FP["fingerprint =<br/>SHA-256(signature ‖ prompt_version ‖ model)"]
  FP --> ACK[("acknowledgements<br/>by fingerprint, TTL")]
  V -.->|operator acks ok/warning| ACK
  ACK -.->|next heartbeat:<br/>known conditions → prompt| PROMPT["Prompt assembly"]
  PROMPT --> SUP{"matches active ack<br/>& unchanged?"}
  SUP -->|yes| HIDE["suppress (return ok)"]
  SUP -->|no| SHOW["re-evaluate"]
